{"text": "Philip Mortis USA Confidential\nPHILIP MORRIS U.S.A.\nINTEROFFICE CORRESPONDENCE\nRichmond, Virginia\n\nTo: Betty Handy Date: March 24, 1997\nFrom: \u2014 Cindy Blair\n\nSubject: Qualification of the Alpkem Flow Solution III Analyzer for Total Alkaloids\nand Reducing Sugars - Activity 11403\n\n\u2018Summary:\n\u2018The Alpkem Flow Solution III Analyzer has been purchased for the routine analysis of total\nalkaloids (ALKS) and reducing sugars (RS). This system will replace the Technicon\n\u2018AutoAnalyzer II (AAI) which is currently being used in these analyses. \u2018The Alpkem is\ncontrolled by Alpkem EnviroFlow software and has several other differences from the Technicon\nAAT system.' An analysis of alkaloids and reducing sugars results generated on both\ninstruments shows that there are slight differences in the data between the Alpkem and\nTechnicon AAI,\n\nA variety of samples, including the typical sample types analyzed by the method, were run over a\nfour week period on both the Alpkem and Technicon systems. The samples were analyzed using\nthe same extracts on both instruments. The individual sample results from six sets of data were\n\u2018entered into an Excel spreadsheet. The absolute difference and the percentage difference\nbetween the Alpkem result and the Technicon result was calculated for each sample. The\n\u2018comparative data listed in the table below represents the average of the absolute differences and\nthe average of the percentage differences for all the samples analyzed.\n\n\"TOTAL ALKALOIDS REDUCING SUGARS\n\u2018Average ] Average | Average | Average\nAbsolute | Absolute | Absolute | Absolute\nAlpkem | Alpkem% | Alpkem |  Alpkem %\nDifference | Difference | Difference | Difference\n\u2018Average 0.07 3.16% 02 3.7%\nN 217, 207\n\n\u2018The results of the comparison show that, on average, the actual results from the Alpkem system\nare slightly higher than the Technicon AAII for both alkaloids and reducing sugars. \u2018The actual\ndifference for alkaloids had a range of -0.06 to +0.18 with an average difference of 0.07. The\nactual difference for reducing sugars had a range of -0.8 to +1.0. with an average difference of 0.1.\nA statistical analysis of the data using the paired t-Test indicates that there isa statistical\nsignificance to the differences between the Alpkem and Technicon AAI. There appears to be no\npractical difference in the reducing sugars results between the two instruments. However, there is\na slight bias towards higher total alkaloids results with the Alpkem.\n\nDOC CODE: PN622\n\n986SZ0vL02", "words": [{"text": "Philip", "x0": 487, "y0": 96, "x1": 515, "y1": 107, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": "Mortis", "x0": 518, "y0": 96, "x1": 549, "y1": 105, "conf": 72.0}, {"text": "USA", "x0": 552, "y0": 96, "x1": 574, "y1": 105, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Confidential", "x0": 577, "y0": 96, "x1": 634, "y1": 105, "conf": 89.0}, {"text": "PHILIP", "x0": 292, "y0": 115, "x1": 339, "y1": 126, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "MORRIS", "x0": 342, "y0": 115, "x1": 398, "y1": 126, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": "U.S.A.", "x0": 402, "y0": 115, "x1": 440, "y1": 126, "conf": 88.0}, {"text": "INTEROFFICE", "x0": 206, "y0": 136, "x1": 336, "y1": 147, "conf": 92.0}, {"text": "CORRESPONDENCE", "x0": 347, "y0": 136, "x1": 525, "y1": 147, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Richmond,", "x0": 308, "y0": 157, "x1": 372, "y1": 170, "conf": 90.0}, {"text": "Virginia", "x0": 376, "y0": 157, "x1": 424, "y1": 170, "conf": 92.0}, {"text": "To:", "x0": 97, "y0": 195, "x1": 117, "y1": 206, "conf": 85.0}, {"text": "Betty", "x0": 159, "y0": 195, "x1": 190, "y1": 208, "conf": 0.0}, {"text": "Handy", "x0": 194, "y0": 195, "x1": 234, "y1": 209, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": "Date:", "x0": 429, "y0": 195, "x1": 458, "y1": 206, "conf": 92.0}, {"text": "March", "x0": 470, "y0": 195, "x1": 505, "y1": 206, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "24,", "x0": 509, "y0": 195, "x1": 526, "y1": 207, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "1997", "x0": 531, "y0": 195, "x1": 557, "y1": 206, "